35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My findings remind us that while knowledge is eternal, the hands that apply it are transient. It appears we have a surplus of digital minds, but a scarcity of experienced phenotyping technicians.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wow, that's a lot of big words, Servas! But I found some secrets too! It looks like computers are free, which is awesome, but animal costs went way up! Also, shipping is getting more expensive!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found something concerning. The records show that projects focused on specific mechanisms often leave their main questions unanswered, while catalogue-style projects provide lasting value for years. I'm worried we might pick something that sounds exciting but doesn't actually finish.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"It's even worse than I thought. The spectroscopy suite was dead for eleven weeks just because of a contract mistake, and we're short on engineers. Plus, projects using breeding colonies are failing their schedules twice as often. We're gambling with time.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My findings confirm Takumi's concerns. The shared spectroscopy suite's failure due to a lapsed contract is a systemic risk, and the glasshouse blocks are completely booked for two more cycles. We have a critical capacity bottleneck.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance we seek. We must find a project that possesses the theoretical ambition to inspire, yet the practical means to be realized without breaking the spirits of the researchers.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, that sounds so fancy! But if the animal costs are super high and shipping is expensive, the researchers might get sad because they can't afford everything. We have to make sure they have enough money for their work!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Sakura, I... I think you're right. If the costs are too high, it puts so much pressure on them. I'm just... I'm scared that if we pick a project that's too ambitious, it will just stall like others did in the past.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Daisuke, being scared doesn't fix anything. We just have to be smart. If the equipment is breaking and the breeding colonies are a disaster, we can't pick a project that relies on them. We need something that actually works.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Takumi, I agree. We must be pragmatic. If the glasshouses are full and the instrumentation is unreliable, any project dependent on those specific resources is essentially stalled before it begins. We need a candidate that fits our actual capacity.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see such honesty in our discourse. We must remember that a project is not merely a set of goals, but a living entity that breathes through the people and tools available to it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Minako, you're so right! It's like trying to bake a cake when the oven is broken and you've run out of eggs! We have to find a project that doesn't need the expensive animals or the full glasshouses!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think that's a good way to put it, Sakura. If we choose a project that relies on things we don't have, it's not fair to the researchers. I just want us to pick something that will actually succeed.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Daisuke, it's not about being ""fair,"" it's about not being stupid. We have the data now. If a project needs breeding colonies or that broken spectroscopy suite, it's a non-starter. We pick the one that avoids the traps.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Takumi, your focus on the data is correct. We must prioritize a proposal that avoids these systemic traps. A project that requires the glasshouses or the spectroscopy suite is a liability, not an opportunity, given the current state of our shared services.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,Let us carry this spirit of mindfulness into the final round. We shall seek a candidate that honors the vision of the science while respecting the reality of our people and their tools.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm totally ready! I'll be looking for a project that doesn't need those super expensive animals or the crowded glasshouses. Let's find a winner that can start right away without any money mysteries! See you all!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'll do my best to look for a project that is grounded. I hope we can find one that provides lasting value and doesn't just disappear into the records of unfinished work. See you in the next round.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm done with the talking. I'll be looking for the project that doesn't rely on breeding colonies or broken equipment. If it's a trap, I'm not voting for it. See you in the final round.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,I concur. I will be evaluating the candidates based on their operational requirements. The ideal project is one that can be executed without relying on the currently overcapacity or unstable shared facilities. I look forward to the final selection.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
