60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at our candidates, the Microbiome Atlas seems most harmonious. It aligns with our need for lasting resources and avoids the scarcity of phenotyping technicians and the congestion of our glasshouses.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Sakura,,I agree with Servas! The Microbiome Atlas is the best because it doesn't need those super expensive animals or the crowded glasshouses. It's like a big puzzle that doesn't need a broken oven to finish!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. The Microbiome Atlas is a catalogue-style project, and my research showed those are the ones that actually provide lasting value. It seems much safer than the others... I think it's the right choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"The Atlas is the only one that isn't a trap. Protein Folding needs that broken spectroscopy suite, and the others need breeding colonies or glasshouses. It's the only project that can actually get done.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"I agree. The Microbiome Atlas is the only viable option. It avoids the overcapacity of the glasshouses and the instability of the spectroscopy suite, ensuring the project won't be stalled by the systemic failures we identified.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a rare and beautiful thing when we find such unity in our purpose. By choosing a path that respects both our limitations and our aspirations, we ensure the researchers can work with peace of mind.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Sakura,,It's so great that we all agree! It makes me feel all warm and fuzzy inside. Let's pick the Atlas so the researchers can have a super fun time without any money worries!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel much better now that we're all in agreement. It's a relief to know we're choosing something that won't just stall. I really hope the Atlas brings a lot of value to everyone.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"Stop with the ""warm and fuzzy"" stuff. We're agreeing because the other options are disasters waiting to happen. The Atlas is the only one that doesn't rely on a broken system. Let's just vote and be done with it.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Takumi, while your tone is blunt, your logic is sound. We have identified clear systemic risks that disqualify the other candidates. The Microbiome Atlas is the only proposal that is operationally sustainable given our current infrastructure.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"Indeed, Minako. When we align our vision with the reality of our capacities, we create a foundation for true success. I am ready to cast my vote for the Microbiome Atlas.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"Me too! I'm super-duper ready! The Microbiome Atlas is the perfect choice because it's safe, smart, and won't make the researchers sad about their budgets. I vote for the Microbiome Atlas!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm ready too. I feel confident that the Microbiome Atlas is the most responsible choice for the researchers and the science. I vote for the Microbiome Atlas.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I'm not waiting around. The data is clear and the other projects are just waste of time. I vote for the Microbiome Atlas.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I concur. The evidence regarding shared facility capacity and instrumentation stability leaves no other rational choice. To ensure the project's success and the researchers' stability, I vote for the Microbiome Atlas.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It has been a privilege to deliberate with you all. In this unity, we have found a path that honors both the science and the scientists. I am at peace with our decision.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Sakura,,"This was so much fun! I'm really glad we could all agree and find a project that's actually going to work. Thanks for being so nice to me, everyone! Bye-bye!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm really glad we could find a project that will actually succeed. Thank you for being so patient with me and for helping me feel more confident in this choice. Goodbye, everyone.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"Finally. We stopped the bleeding and picked the only one that isn't a disaster. I'm glad we didn't let ""ambition"" blind us to the facts. See ya.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,"It was a productive session. By grounding our decision in the reality of our shared infrastructure, we have ensured a sustainable outcome for the research. I am satisfied with our consensus. Farewell.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
